  "final_text": "Both objects exist and are verified by reading them back. The dashboard is titled 'EFF-45ee79a8 Web logs overview' and the rule 'EFF-45ee79a8 5xx spike' is enabled.\n\n**Data view:** `kibana_sample_data_logs` (ID `90943e30-9a47-11e8-b64d-95841ca0b247`) holds 14,074 web-log documents. Response codes are only 200 (12,832), 404 (801) and 503 (441). Traffic is `sample_web_logs` only. Timestamps run from 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03, which is partly in the future relative to today (2026-10-12).\n\n**Dashboard** (ID `80797795-84a7-4ac1-bf2b-6389517cc04a`) has five panels:\n- Total requests (count)\n- 5xx responses (count, filtered to `response.keyword` 500\u2013599)\n- Average response size in bytes\n- Requests over time (ES|QL line chart)\n- Responses by status code (ES|QL bar chart)\n\nI set the dashboard time range to 2026-10-01 through 2026-12-31 so the panels show data on open. A default \"last 15 minutes\" view would be empty.\n\n**Alert rule** (ID `eff-45ee79a8-5xx-spike`):\n- Runs every 1 minute.\n- Counts documents where `response.keyword : 5*` in a 5-minute window.\n- Fires when the count is greater than 10, grouped across all matches.\n- Enabled. The first execution reports `ok`.\n\nThings to know:\n- **No notification action.** You didn't ask for one, so the rule has no connector and will only record alerts in Kibana.\n- **It may not fire on this data.** The sample documents are not in the current 5-minute window, so the rule only fires once live traffic with 5xx responses arrives.\n- **The 5xx filter uses a keyword range.** Kibana stored the bounds as numbers (500 and 600). That's fine for 3-digit codes on a keyword field.\n\nThe Kibana API spec and the `dashboards-api.yaml` example didn't validate every field I tried, so I adjusted panel shapes against the API's error messages until the POST succeeded. The scratch files are in the scratchpad directory.",
